I've finally got my first decent game of 3.1 going.  It is a lot of fun, as
most of the good stuff in 3.1 isn't to be found until you get a decent
character going!  (although I really like the new box/bag code, makes life much
easier).

Anyway, Termite the Archeologist is doing quite well.  Due to the scads of neat
toys you can find in this new version, he has taken to piling
spares/nonessential items in a chest, and letting the chest sit near the stairs
while exploring a new level.

Termite has also got himself a pet Black Naga named Ophid.  Ophid is a pretty
sizable pet - he offed a shopkeeper without breaking a sweat, and can tote
around most anything.  The problem is that includes Termite's chest named "good
stuff".  Ophid picked up the chest, and promptly stepped onto a level teleport
trap!  Bye bye pet and a lot of cool stuff.

A level or two later Termite runs into a Gaurdian Naga.  Ah, a good replacement
for Ophid!  Termite befriends the naga named Ralph.  However, go down a level
into a dark room.  Termite is fighting a luecrotta.  A grey dragon shows up!
Uh-oh.  Then the Dragon named Ralph shreds the luecrotta.  It turns out that
Ralph was merely a cross dressing chameleon!  Unfortunately, Ralph decides it'd
be neato-keen to try xorn-ness for a while, then forgets that it's a bad idea
to un-xorn while in a wall.  He died as I tried to dig him out :(

Luckily I have found Ophid and the chest-o-goodies a couple levels later, and
am happily hacking on.

